<div class="callout"><span class="callout__title">Note</span><strong>The drawer decision that matters most:</strong><p>Upgrade your 3 most-used drawers (near hob, near prep zone, cutlery drawer) to tandem boxes with soft-close. Keep the remaining drawers as ball-bearing telescopic. This "3+rest" approach costs ₹12,000–₹20,000 extra vs. all-roller, but transforms the kitchen from "builder-grade" to "premium-feel" where it matters most.</div>
<h2>Pull-Out Accessories — The Specialized Organizers</h2>
<p>Beyond the structural drawers and corner solutions, these purpose-built pull-outs solve specific Indian kitchen problems. Each one targets a workflow pain point.</p>
<p>🌶️</p>
<h4>Masala / Spice Pull-Out</h4>
<p>Angled-tier organizer for Indian spice boxes</p>
<p>₹2,500–₹5,500per unit</p>
<p>A narrow pull-out (200–300mm wide) with 3–4 angled tiers designed for small spice containers, masala dabbas and condiment bottles. Mounts adjacent to the hob for one-hand access while cooking. The angled shelves display labels front-facing so you see every spice without pulling the tray out fully.</p>
<p>🍳</p>
<h4>Pan &amp; Tawa Vertical Divider</h4>
<p>Stores pans vertically instead of stacked</p>
<p>₹1,200–₹3,000per unit</p>
<p>Vertical wire dividers inside a deep base cabinet that hold pans, tawas, cutting boards and baking trays on edge — like books on a shelf. Pull out one pan without unstacking everything above it. A simple but high-impact organizer for Indian kitchens with multiple tawas and kadhai.</p>
<p>🧹</p>
<h4>Broom &amp; Cleaning Pull-Out</h4>
<p>Concealed vertical storage for mops, brooms, cleaning supplies</p>
<p>₹3,000–₹6,500per unit</p>
<p>A narrow tall pull-out (200–300mm wide, full cabinet height) with hooks and clips for brooms, mops, dusters and a lower basket for cleaning liquids. Keeps everything concealed and organized in a 200mm wall gap that would otherwise be dead space.</p>
<p>🔪</p>
<h4>Chopping Board Pull-Out</h4>
<p>Built-in cutting surface that slides out from the countertop</p>
<p>₹1,500–₹3,500per unit</p>
<p>A food-grade chopping board mounted on telescopic runners just below the countertop. Slides out when you need extra prep surface, slides back in when you're done — adding work area without using permanent counter space. Made from food-safe plastic or bamboo.</p>
