<h2>The Kitchen Storage Priority Matrix — What to Buy First</h2>
<p>If your budget doesn't cover every accessory, use this priority order. Each tier adds measurable daily convenience — but the "Essential" tier alone solves 80% of kitchen storage frustration.</p>
<h4>Cutlery Tray + Tandem Drawers × 2 + Dustbin Pull-Out</h4>
<p>The three items that eliminate the top daily kitchen frustrations: mixed-up utensils, unreachable base cabinet depths, and a freestanding dustbin. These alone transform kitchen workflow.</p>
<p>₹8,000–₹18,000 (Hettich)</p>
<h4>Bottle Pull-Out + Corner Carousel</h4>
<p>Reclaims the two most wasted spaces: the narrow gap near the hob (bottles) and the dead corner (carousel). Together they add 15–20% usable storage.</p>
<p>₹6,000–₹14,000 (Hettich)</p>
<h4>Tall Unit (Pantry) + Under-Sink Organizer</h4>
<p>The tall unit is the single biggest capacity add. The under-sink organizer reclaims the most commonly wasted spot. Together they can double accessible kitchen storage.</p>
<p>₹20,000–₹50,000</p>
<h4>Magic Corner (replace carousel) + Masala Pull-Out</h4>
<p>The magic corner is a carousel-level upgrade that changes corner usability entirely. The masala pull-out puts spices at arm's reach during cooking — small cost, daily convenience.</p>
<p>₹14,000–₹33,000</p>
<h4>Lift-Up Wall Shutters + Pull-Down Shelf + Pan Dividers</h4>
<p>These refine an already well-organized kitchen. Lift-ups improve overhead access, pull-down shelves eliminate step-stools, pan dividers end stacking. Worth it if you've covered Essentials and Recommended tiers.</p>
<p>₹12,000–₹30,000</p>
<h4>Chopping Board Pull-Out + Towel Pull-Out + Inner Drawers</h4>
<p>Finishing touches that add prep convenience and visual cleanliness. Inner drawers (drawer-within-drawer) are a luxury — practical only in 600mm+ deep tandem boxes.</p>
<p>₹4,000–₹15,000</p>
