<h2>7 Modular Kitchen Storage Mistakes (and What to Do Instead)</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Spending on accessories before carcass quality.</strong> A ₹28,000 Hafele magic corner inside a ₹1,200-per-sheet MR plywood carcass will last 3 years before the cabinet warps around it. Prioritize BWP/BWR carcass → then hardware → then accessories.</li>
  <li><strong>Using corner carousels when you can afford a magic corner.</strong> Carousels lose 20–30% of corner space and items fall off the edges. If your budget allows a single upgrade, replacing the carousel with a magic corner gives the biggest daily-use improvement.</li>
  <li><strong>Installing lift-up shutters on every wall cabinet.</strong> Lift-up mechanisms cost ₹3,500–₹12,000 per shutter. Use them on the 2–3 most-accessed wall cabinets. The rest can use standard hinged doors at ₹400–₹800 per pair.</li>
  <li><strong>Skipping the tall unit to save money.</strong> A tall unit costs ₹18,000–₹45,000 but replaces 3–4 wall cabinets and provides 3–5× the storage density. It's a net savings if you reduce wall cabinet count accordingly.</li>
  <li><strong>Choosing all-roller drawers to cut costs.</strong> Roller runners degrade in 3–5 years — the drawers stick, squeak and sag. Spend ₹1,200–₹3,000 more per drawer on ball-bearing telescopic runners. The extra ₹8,000–₹15,000 for a full kitchen extends smooth operation by 8–10 years.</li>
  <li><strong>Not planning pull-out slots during layout design.</strong> Bottle pull-outs, masala pull-outs and broom pull-outs need specific width slots (150–300mm) designed into the layout before carcass fabrication. Retrofitting is expensive and often impossible.</li>
  <li><strong>Mixing hardware brands.</strong> A kitchen with Hettich tandem drawers, Ebco hinges and Hafele channels will have three different soft-close feels, three different warranties and three different replacement part ecosystems. Standardize on one brand for all mechanisms.</li>
</ol>
